---
// The 3Rivers dossier. Hand-built rather than generated, because it carries a
// diagram and a manager endorsement the coursework pages do not. Copy is
// byte-identical to what the modal carried.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import TechnicalLayout from '../../components/technical/TechnicalLayout.astro';
import SystemsJoinDiagram from '../../components/work/diagrams/SystemsJoinDiagram.astro';
---

<Base
  title="3Rivers Federal Credit Union · Michael Doerffler"
  description="A mortgage inquiry intelligence report built on protected member data at a federally regulated credit union, shaped directly with the team that uses it."
  ogImage="/og/technical-3rivers.png"
>
  <TechnicalLayout label="DATA ENGINEERING &amp; BI · REGULATED FINANCIAL INSTITUTION" title="3Rivers Federal Credit Union" wide>
    <div class="sec-label">DATA ENGINEERING &amp; BI · REGULATED FINANCIAL INSTITUTION</div>
    <h1 class="tp-title">3Rivers Federal Credit Union</h1>

    <div class="tp-cols">
      <p class="tp-body-text">
        3Rivers is a federally regulated credit union: real member data, enterprise systems, and
        compliance obligations, staffed by people who had been doing data, AI, and finance work for
        years. I spent a summer there as a Business Intelligence intern, working close to the data
        layer on protected systems.
      </p>
      <p class="tp-body-text">
        It was also the room where I was the least experienced person present. I spent it asking
        questions, absorbing how experienced practitioners scope problems and handle data, and
        carrying what I learned directly into the internship I was running in parallel that same
        summer.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tp-proj">
      <div>
        <p class="tp-status">SHIPPED</p>
        <h2 class="tp-proj-title">Mortgage Inquiry Intelligence Report</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="tp-body-text">
          Delivered in Power BI. Joined SavvyMoney mortgage alerts with member and loan officer
          data across three enterprise systems (Alkami, Exasol, network files), cleaning and
          reconciling mismatched schemas in Power Query, normalizing SSN fields and identifiers. I
          set up meetings with the mortgage team to learn what would make it genuinely valuable to
          them, then took their feedback and iterated, building a tool they'd actually want to
          use, giving officers early visibility into members shopping for a mortgage.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="spec-block">
      <p class="spec-line"><span class="spec-key">STACK</span> Power BI · Power Query · Exasol</p>
      <p class="spec-line"><span class="spec-key">METHOD</span> Stakeholder-driven build with the mortgage team · multi-source sourcing · schema reconciliation · normalized identifiers across mismatched schemas</p>
    </div>

    <SystemsJoinDiagram />

    <div class="endorse">
      <p class="endorse-label">FROM MY MANAGER</p>
      <p class="endorse-body">
        "Michael is exceptionally adaptive, with a keen ability to quickly assess new situations
        and respond effectively. He is a proactive communicator who ensures he understands project
        scopes before execution and follows up after delivery to ensure outcomes were achieved.
        Also, his positive energy helps assure a great team vibe, making him a great addition to
        any team."
      </p>
      <p class="endorse-attr">Chad Gramling, AVP Business Intelligence</p>
    </div>
  </TechnicalLayout>
</Base>
